{"name":"Full of Beans","hex":"#884d04","fetched":"2026-10-23","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"full of beans","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Energetic and enthusiastic."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Incorrect; uninformed; exaggerating or expressing falsehood."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/full_of_beans"}],"entries":[{"title":"Timothy Goes to School","blocks":[{"text":"Timothy Goes to School is a preschool children's animated television series developed by Kate Barris and based on books by Rosemary Wells. The series was produced by Nelvana Limited and Animation Services Limited in association with Silver Lining Entertainment Limited for TVOntario and PBS, and with the participation of Knowledge Network, Access and Saskatchewan Communications Network (SCN)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/e/ef/Timothy_Goes_to_School_Logo.png/330px-Timothy_Goes_to_School_Logo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timothy_Goes_to_School","wikidata":"Q1885979"},{"title":"Bean","blocks":[{"text":"A bean is the seed of plants in many genera of the legume family (Fabaceae) used as a vegetable for human consumption or animal feed. The seeds are sold fresh or preserved through drying (a pulse). Beans have been cultivated since the seventh millennium BCE in Thailand, and since the second millennium BCE in Europe and in Peru. Most beans, with the exception of peas, are summer crops. As legumes, the plants fix nitrogen and form seeds with a high protein content. They are produced on a scale of millions of tons annually in many countries, with India as the largest producer."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/French_beans_J1.JPG/330px-French_beans_J1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bean","wikidata":"Q379813"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://t